{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Who are these men with you?</b> We find the expression ״מִי״ that is not an interrogative but is said in contempt, as it is written (I Samuel 25:10): ״וַיַּעַן נָבָל אֶת עַבְדֵי דָוִד מִי דָוִד וּמִי בֶן יִשַׁי״ — that is, who is he; he is accounted as nothing. So the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Balaam, whose spirit was haughty: ״Who are these men״ — these inferior ones? Are they worthy to be with you, that you should go with them? And he answered: ״Balak son of Zippor king of Moab sent me״ — and a servant of a king is like a king. Nevertheless he said: ״HaShem refused to let me go with you״ — but with officials greater than you."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:42:27.962005451Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}